    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// A piece may declare its own finite data and fold over it. Nothing here is" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// built in: `Gesture` is three constructors this file names, and" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// `gesture_fold` is the one structural fold the declaration generates — a case" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// per constructor, and the recursive fields already folded" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// (docs/rules/language/02-core-calculus.md §1)." },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "//" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// What it buys is that the *plan* is a value. A gesture can be built, passed," },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// and matched before any music exists, and the same plan reads two ways: as" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// notation, by folding it into `Music`, and as a count, by folding it into a" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// number. A `Music -> Music` function could do neither." },
    { "kind": "piece", "text": "piece" },
